==Trivia==
*Booklet Islands has multiple writing-related puns in its Japanese names:
**The sub-chapter's Japanese name, Bukku Rettō (ブック列島, "Book Archipelago"), is a pun on ブックレット ''bukkuretto'' (booklet) and 列島 ''rettō'' (archipelago).
**[[Dictionary Estate]]'s Japanese name, Dikushonarī Jisho, (ディクショナリー地所, "Dictionary Estate"), plays off of how 辞書 (the Japanese word for dictionary) and 地所 (estate) are both read as ''jisho''.
**[[Temple of Manga]]'s Japanese name, Ma-Ga Jiin (マ=ガ寺院, "Ma-Ga Temple"), is a pun on マガジン ''magajin'' (magazine) and 寺院 ''jiin'' (temple). The presence of [[Othom]] may be related to how ガ ''ga'' can mean moth.

